":329},"usage","Usage",[332,333,335],"h3",{"id":334},"loading-and-empty-data","Loading and empty data",[304,337,338,341,342,345],{},[308,339,340],{},"loading"," means a query is in progress. When re-querying with existing data, the data fades and switches with a height transition; without data, the query shows \"Loading…\". After the data is cleared, ",[308,343,344],{},"empty"," is shown, \"No data\" by default.",[347,348],"component-example",{"name":349},"table-basic",[304,351,352,353,356],{},"Keep the existing ",[308,354,355],{},"data"," while re-querying and update it after the query succeeds, so the data fades instead of being cleared.",[332,358,360],{"id":359},"first-load-skeleton","First-load skeleton",[304,362,363,364,366,367,370],{},"When the component is created while loading (",[308,365,340],{}," is ",[308,368,369],{},"true",") with no data, three skeleton rows are shown based on the number of columns; after the first query finishes, the skeleton is no longer shown. Press \"Recreate\" to recreate the table in the loading state.",[347,372],{"name":373},"table-skeleton",[304,375,376,377,380],{},"The skeleton column count uses leaf columns and excludes columns hidden by ",[308,378,379],{},"tableProps.state.columnVisibility",".",[304,382,383,384,387,388,391,392,387,395,398,399,402,403,406,407,410,411,380],{},"Set the row count with ",[308,385,386],{},"skeleton-rows"," (default ",[308,389,390],{},"3",", at least 1 row), and the height and other styles of each skeleton bar with ",[308,393,394],{},"skeleton-class",[308,396,397],{},"h-6",", i.e. 24px), which replaces the default as a whole. Both can be set site-wide with ",[308,400,401],{},"components.table.skeletonRows"," and ",[308,404,405],{},"components.table.skeletonClass"," in ",[317,408,42],{"href":409},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fcomponent-defaults",", and also apply to ",[308,412,320],{},[414,415,420],"pre",{"className":416,"code":417,"language":418,"meta":419,"style":419},"language-vue shiki s